  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as both a noun and a suru verb. The negative form {断言|だんげん}できない (cannot say for certain) is particularly common, as speakers often hedge their statements. When used in the positive, it conveys strong conviction and personal responsibility for the claim.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {断言|だんげん}する: to declare, to assert\n- {断言|だんげん}できない: cannot say for certain\n- {断言|だんげん}を{避|さ}ける: to avoid making a definitive statement\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {明言|めいげん}: clear statement (similar force but less emotional weight)\n- {宣言|せんげん}: declaration (more official, public-facing)",
